'''Nagumi''', also known as '''Ngong''' (Gong), is an extinct [[Jarawan languages|Jarawan]] language of the [[North Province (Cameroon)|North Province]] of [[Cameroon]]. It had only two fluent speakers in 1983 and only one in 1995.{{Citation needed|date=September 2022}}

